<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Order of Battle against the Alans</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 135</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a> · Also known as Ektaxis kata Alanon, Acies contra Alanos</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Order of Battle against the Alans is a short Greek military treatise by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arrian">Arrian</a>, governor of Cappadocia, written around 135 CE when an Alan invasion threatened the province. It describes how he would march and deploy his legions and auxiliaries, with infantry in a deep formation to receive the charge of the Alans' <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heavy-cavalry">heavy cavalry</a>. It is a rare first-hand account of a Roman field army's dispositions.</p></div>
